# LiteLLM routing configuration, RENDERED by Ansible onto the managed node.
#
# No SPDX header: like the compose template, this is written onto the node rather than kept here.
#
# #2, v1 SCOPE: tigerblue77's own account only. Dragnix adds his own models later, from "/ui" himself
# -- his own decision, matching how he already runs every other self-hosted database of this estate
# (deployed empty, populated live). What #2 asks beyond this -- "access_groups"-backed teams and
# virtual keys created by idempotent Ansible tasks against LiteLLM's admin API, per-key rpm/tpm
# limits, the "sci-*" / "gen-*" sensitivity split, and the executable cross-account negative test --
# is real and still open; it is deliberately NOT attempted here. Every entry below already carries
# "model_info.access_groups: [\"tigerblue77\"]" so that work has one less thing to retrofit.
